Hi all,

The hardware security keys arrived (two per person, 24 total, $1,104 on the ops card). They're in named envelopes on my desk; take yours whenever you're in this week.

Setup takes about four minutes:
1. Google Workspace > Security > 2-Step Verification > Add security key. Enroll both keys (one stays at home).
2. GitHub > Settings > Password and authentication > Security keys. Same two keys.
3. Put the spare somewhere that is not the same bag as your laptop.

Phone prompts keep working alongside the keys until mid-April; after that the keys become the only second factor, which is the control our compliance file asks for. I'll send one more reminder in April; nobody is being switched over without notice.

Arjun has offered to help anyone who gets stuck, and Kofi has already volunteered to be the person who loses a key first.

